npn 7p-7a (see also carevue flownotes for objective data)

dx: 38 yo fe w/ crohns, immunosupressed d/t RX of mtx;
admitted to [**Hospital1 2**] [**7-21**] for SOB, cough, fever;
pt has colostomy w/ pigtail drain;

admitted for tx of pna;
out to floor [**7-23**], returned [**7-24**] 12n for episode SOB/dyspnea/hypoxia earlier in the a.m.;

[**2040-7-22**] pt NAD in [**Wardname **]4, only on nc O2 at 2 l; b/p stable;
however [**7-25**] at 06:45 pt noted to have change in cardiac rhythm--pt previously NSR, at 06:45 [**7-25**] pt w/ ? lack of QRS after 'p' waves per cardiac monitor breifly, then rhythm changed to sinus arrythmia; b/p stable, O2 sat stable w/ only mild subtle decrease overnight;
   EKG done, MD stated pt had had question of clot vs PICC tip in RA;
had chest CT [**7-25**], which confirmed significant pulmonary emboli--pt received IV bolus heparin at 19:30 than started on hep gtt as ordered at 1150 u/hr;  PTT drawn at approx 02:15--result 132.4, hep gtt of x 1 hr, then decreased by 250 u/hr according to heparin gtt protocol as ordered;

neuro/pain:
a/o x3; hx anxiety, bipolar--pt on zyprexia, ritalin, methadone;
pt w/ apparent physiological tolerance of narcotic dilaudid--is ordered for, requests, and receives 4-8 mg IV q 2-4 hrs;
  pt has had 'chest/pleuritic' pain for a few days, has chronic pain d/t chrohn's;

c-v/resp:
NSR, sinus arrhythmia at times, does become somewhat tachycardic when OOB to commode, also mild increase in resp rate noted; O2 sat remains adequate w/ nc O2 in use; crackles heard rt lung;

g-i/nutrition/FS's:
receives TPN as ordered;
pt w/ colostomy and pigtail drain;
requested and received cream of wheat apprx 19:00;
pt provided w/ towels and chux to empty colostomy bag;
on q 6 hr FS w/ SS coverage--occasionally requires a couple units of reg insulin--also depends if pt has eating alot of candy or food w/ sugar; pt currently remains on steroids;

g-u:
excellent urine output--large volume d/t large volume IV Abx's;

access:
unable to draw labs off PICC yesterday a.m.; pt Very difficult periph IV stick for labs;
  received left EJ yesterday for chest CT; currently has heparin gtt running into;

skin:
pt on contact precautions for hx [**Name (NI) 414**] and MRSA

PLAN:
1) continue abx as ordered
2) remain in ICU d/t nature of pulmonary emboli
3) possible continued cardiac w/u
4) follow for any continued s/s resp distress
5) check results a.m. labs

npn 7p-7a (see also carevue flowtones for objective data)

dx: LGIB
met CA

pt received IVF bolus as ordered yester eve, pt's afib increased in v-response and decreased in O2 sat; team resident ordered another 250 cc IVF bolus, pt continued to have increased v-response even to 150's and up to 160, w/ continued decrease in O2 sat to approx 84/85;
   stat p-cxr showed whiteout left lung, and rt lower, suggesting pulm edema; ordered for and received morphine, lopressor, lasix, ntg topical; pt finally improved approx 01:00;
   goal for the rest of the night was to keep pt as comfortable as possible to prevent further flashes of pulm edema; received several doses of morphine sulfate 2 mg IV;

other:
shingles remain current, left rib area, small amount serous drainage;

hct stable suggesting no further GIB;

plt ct continues to decrease, this am 70 thousand;

pt afebrile overnight;

pt's sister stayed overnight;

pt continues to INSIST to be postioned on rt side; attempted to reposition to rt to relieve pressure on left hip skin, pt scooted to back, then to right;

after the 3-4 hr of pulm edema crisis, pt received approx 2 mg IV morhpine sulfate every hr to maintaain pt's comfort and rest;

PLAN:
1) pt's condition continues to suggest limited options in treatment and response; as stated in chart, CMO status may become more appropriate

2) ?transfer to regular floor bed
3) strongly suggest IV drip morhpine sulfate
4) suggest cease q 4 hr hcts unless pt becomes symptomatic for bleeding
5) no stool this shift; send c-diff spec when stools
6) position on left side with ocaasional relief of pressure from left side
7) shingles precautions

