npn 19:30- 07:00 (see also carevue flownotes for objective data)

dx: RLL pna; NSTEMI
    resp failure; thrombocytosis; decrs'd LOC;

88 yo married male, resident of [**Hospital 212**] Rehab, supportive family;
c/c increasing lethargy and SOB 3 days prior to admission, w/ poor po intake;
pt's baseline is w/c, feeds self pureed food/thickened liquids;

ER w/u showed RLL pna per CXR and NSTEMI re elevated troponin to 1.18 w/ EKG changes per card c/s;

NEURO:
pt reportedly essentially unresponsive in ER, remained same at arrival to MICU at 19:30, limbs stiff but w/out movement;

C-V:
[**Hospital 197**] w/out vasopressors so far; IVF's started at 12a D5 [**12-26**] at 125 cc/hr; hrt rhythm a-fib, w/ controlled v-response in low 10's;
extremities cold, bilat from knees down, hands warm at beginning of shift, cooler later in the shift--lost good pleth for O2 sat monitoring;
22:40 troponin 1.14, down from 1.18; MB Index up slightly to 17.5% from 10.3%;

resp:
ABG done at 00:15, showed pCO2 continuned to be in low 70's, therefore placed on facial mask ventilation to try to assist pt to blow off CO2; oxygenation has not shown to be a problem so far;

G-I:
pt NPO for now; started on IV PPI;
unable to take any PO meds d/t unresponsiveness;

G-U:
urine output very low first 4 hrs here in MICU, did increase some midway through shift; Urine speciment sent off for analysis and cx as ordered;

skin:
pt received full bedbath; no bedsores seen;
came w/ 2 PIV's; one in each forearm;

musculoskeletal;
pt stiff d/t age; rt foot appears chronically/permanently turned in;

PLAN:
1) pt DNR/DNI
2) continue to treat pt medically
3) IV Abx
4) mask ventilation to try to assist pt to blow off CO2
5) obtain sputum for gm stain and cx when able
6) check results a.m. labs

